{
 "_doc": [
  "HW1 tweak params -> AE player skills (players/<class>/skills/<skill>.sval).",
  "A ladder is one HW1 upgrade chain ('hw1': upgrade ids without their trailing number) and the AE skill, or modifier skill ('mod': id, or index for id-less ones), whose levels are the same tiers.",
  "'after' names the unlock ladder whose values are this ladder's tier 0. 'unlock' is the bool param (or 'param>0') that owns the skill.",
  "params: HW1 param -> [AE key, conversion]. The key is 'bind:<name>' or a plain skill param; null means AE has no equivalent. The conversion is only used for values that sit on no HW1 tier: id, pct (/100), ms (s -> ms), x16 (tiles -> px), inv (1/x), inv1000 (1000/x), lin a b (a*x+b), ratio (scaled by AE/HW1 tier 0), interp (through the tier pairs), snap (nearest tier: AE keeps it in a buff file).",
  "base: params no HW1 upgrade changes -> [skill, AE key, conversion], or null.",
  "Paired by shop category and level, which AE kept from HW1 for every class."
 ],
